=======================================================================
Third-party components and source attribution
=======================================================================

The MIT text above covers RaMA-G's original code. Separately licensed
components below retain their own terms; this section does not relicense
them. Full bundled license texts and per-file notices remain with the sources.
Installation copies the applicable dependency licenses into share/ramag.

RaMA-derived centromere code: Apache-2.0, copyright 2024
MALABZ_UESTC Pinglu Zhang. Source: https://github.com/pinglu-zhang/RaMA,
commit 7bc89c4902bc9254f18cc4b05c4bf491a10bd7cb.
See third_party/rama/LICENSE and original notices in third_party/rama/core.
Local changes provide library ownership, checked coordinates, deterministic
unknown-base handling, cancellation and memory safety. Modified files retain
prominent modification notices. Original reference snapshots are not required
by the production build.

RaMAx-derived pairwise code: MIT, copyright 2026 Pinglu Zhang. Source:
https://github.com/pinglu-zhang/RaMAx,
revision 7d08359e0df7f7e6ffcfe67217c3399761cb2129.
The extracted pairwise anchor, cluster, connection, alignment and CIGAR code
uses checked 64-bit coordinates and owned library records; coordinate and DP
comparison corrections are retained. Graph/multispecies orchestration is not
part of this component. The same revision supplied kseq and spdlog snapshots.

KSW2: MIT; see third_party/ksw2/LICENSE and upstream notices in its sources.
kseq: MIT, copyright Attractive Chaos; its complete notice remains embedded
in third_party/kseq/kseq.h and is included with installed license materials.
spdlog: MIT, copyright 2016 Gabi Melman; see third_party/spdlog/LICENSE.
Embedded fmt has its own MIT notice, reproduced below and retained in headers.

Sufkit: MIT, copyright 2026 sufkit contributors. Source:
https://github.com/malabz/sufkit,
commit 028075e6f2d622fcbdcf76b153bbde0f069ca64f.
Its license and licenses shipped for bundled parlaylib, kseq, CaPS-SA,
libdivsufsort and SDSL accompany the installed dependency materials.
RaMA-G does not directly depend on SeqPro.

WFA2: MIT; source https://github.com/smarco/WFA2-lib,
commit 99a5879a3a2972eff168cbcc6610b6cf02844ed0.
Its license is installed when the centromere backend is enabled. Four patched
translation units in third_party/rama/wfa_safety preserve upstream notices
and replace unaligned accesses and an undefined empty-trace shift without
changing alignment penalties or heuristic defaults.

Centrolign kernel subset: MIT; source https://github.com/jeizenga/centrolign,
commit a604cbdcff2e22e643fc9e17d4679296ee5e42fe.
See third_party/centrolign_stitch/LICENSE. Local changes isolate namespaces,
account for scoped kernel allocations, add cooperative interruption and use
an equivalent allocation-free iterative gcd. Only fixed-endpoint linear-graph
DP and unpruned wavefront kernels are integrated; anchoring and graph merging
are not imported. Original copyright notices remain in source files.

